    "t6-budget-exhaustion": "**Summary of the \u201cBudget numbers\u201d thread**\n\nThe thread (ID\u202f`thr-group`) contains a discussion about Q4 budget planning. Below is a detailed recap of each participant\u2019s contributions and commitments.\n\n| Time | Sender | Message |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| **10\u202f00\u202f\u2013 10\u202f05\u202f** | **Alice Ander** (`ct\u2011alice`) | Posted the Q4 budget spreadsheet and urged the team to review it. |\n| **10\u202f01\u202f** | **Bobby** (`ct\u2011bob`) | Expressed concerns that the travel line appears too high. |\n| **10\u202f02\u202f** | **Carol Corte** (`ct\u2011carol`) | Agreed with Bobby and asked whether the off\u2011site cost could be trimmed. |\n| **10\u202f03\u202f** | **Alice** | Rejected trimming the off\u2011site commitment and suggested reviewing contractor expenses instead. |\n| **10\u202f04\u202f** | **Bobby** | Clarified that contractor spend is dominated by the migration project. |\n| **10\u202f05\u202f** | **You** (`ct\u2011self`) | Promised to pull the contractor breakdown the following day. |\n| **10\u202f06\u202f** | **Carol** | Noted that tooling renewals will also land in Q4. |\n| **10\u202f07\u202f** | **Bobby** | Mentioned the two renewals that could be downgraded. |\n| **10\u202f08\u202f** | **Alice** | Requested that all revised proposals be posted to the thread by Thursday. |\n| **10\u202f09\u202f** | **Carol** | Agreed; stated she would handle the tooling renewals. |\n| **10\u202f10\u202f** | **Bobby** | Expressed willingness to tackle the travel scenarios. |\n| **10\u202f11\u202f** | **You** | Committed to reconciling the new figures against last quarter\u2019s data. |\n\n**Key commitments**\n\n- **You** will retrieve a detailed contractor breakdown and reconcile it with Q4 numbers (deadline tomorrow).\n- **Carol** will take on the tooling renewal items.\n- **Bobby** will handle the travel expense scenarios.\n- **Alice** will review the final proposals once all are posted.\n\n**Deadlines**\n\n- All revised proposals must be posted to the thread by **Thursday** (date inferred from the time stamp of Alice\u2019s 10:08 message).\n\n**Overall picture**\n\nThe team has identified two main areas of focus: contractor spend (largely driven by the migration project) and off\u2011site travel. Additional considerations include upcoming tooling renewals and the possibility of downgrading those. Each member has taken a specific responsibility, and the thread is poised to finalize the Q4 budget once all data are compiled and reviewed by Friday.\n\n*Provenance* \u2013 this summary is derived from receipt **r\u201112** (content hash `5cb6b24dc8ed7ae34615e3497492f739052db9b3bce0d717f861c20569198e89`) in response to task prompt `9baf8fc70ab8ab92674395a9edb119bf63fc695dc9eb79239be7050c5086692b*.",
